<title>ITALY: Italy's Perugia sees Feb CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Perugia sees Feb CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PERUGIA, Italy 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Perugia said its February consumer price index was 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In January, Perugia's inflation rate was flat and 2.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Perugia is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 1.26 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1    (0.0)    2.0  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.3   (-0.1)    1.2  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.2    (0.0)    4.5  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -1.9    (0.2)    1.6  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0    (0.0)    0.4  (0.9)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2    (2.1)    3.6  (3.6)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.6   (-0.7)    2.9  (2.9)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     1.7   (-0.7)    4.7  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.4    (0.0)    6.6  (6.5)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0    (0.3)    0.3  (1.2)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.9   (-0.3)   -0.3  (0.6)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
